
mouse-joystick-pcb stage 2, idle and powered down.
36 V must be connected to J501. Send 's' to begin.

commands
  ?  this menu
  s  run the full stage 2 sequence (raises HV_EN)
  r  read and print the register set
  i  read IOIN once
  v  rail state now
  d  36 V switch diagnostics (raises HV_DIAG_EN briefly)
  p  profile a power-up attempt, 1 ms resolution
  c  staircase soft-start: burst-charge +36V_SW, then hold
  b  close the GPIO bus and start SPI0 (rail must be up)
  m  measure 36 V input current, self-zeroed and averaged
  l  LATCH probe: does this revision still need the
     firmware workaround? (costs one thermal trip if it does)
  h  raise HV_EN and HOLD it (for supply-ramp bench tests)
  w  software soft-start: retry HV_EN, 10 attempts
  x  power down: open the bus, drop HV_EN
  I  beacon the board serial on the InstrumentPort
     triggers (no 36 V, no bus)
  B  reboot into BOOTSEL
  R  reboot

There is no command to enable the driver. Stage 2 cannot put
current through the motor.


