##### send 'l' at +24.4 s
LATCH probe: a plain single-shot HV_EN assertion.
  On pcb v1.0 LATCH is GP24 through R503. The probe drives it
  HIGH first to reproduce the strapped behaviour of v0.1-v0.3
  (expect FAIL: latch-off trips while charging 208 uF), then
  'p'/powerUp() holds it LOW for the ramp, which should PASS
  and report the direct method, for the first time on any
  board. Record both outcomes in the PCB bring-up log.

  rail came up:  yes
  rail held:     no
  held for:      13 ms of 250 ms
  rail peak:     3.293 V
